{
  "why": [
    "The arrangement is resolved TWICE, in two languages, on purpose: the server",
    "resolves it for design_read_layout (ruling 3 — the answer is the arrangement",
    "as the panel shows it, not the document), and the client keeps resolving it",
    "locally because the Pages panel renders optimistically, before any round trip",
    "(`resolveRouteOrder` in v2_fe/src/lib/design-layout.ts, `groupedPages` in",
    "v2_fe/src/pages/design/pages-order.ts, mirrored by `resolve_route_order` and",
    "`panel_sections` in backend/plugins/taskflow-design/src/layout_doc.rs).",
    "",
    "That duplication is structural, but UNPINNED duplication is not: both rule",
    "sets have already changed once (pages-order.ts records a wrong earlier move",
    "rule and a changed section-drawing rule), and prose naming the other",
    "implementation cannot fail when the two drift apart.",
    "",
    "So there is ONE table of cases and TWO readers of it, and a one-sided change",
    "to either rule set turns this file red on that side:",
    "  * backend/plugins/taskflow-design/tests/layout_doc.rs (via include_str!)",
    "  * v2_fe/src/pages/design/layout-panel-cases.test.ts (via readFileSync)",
    "",
    "`doc` is a layout document exactly as the server stores and sends it",
    "(`layout_doc::LayoutDoc`), `manifest` is the project's route list in manifest",
    "order, and `expect` is the panel's answer: the FLOW, the groups with their",
    "pages, and the pages no group claims. Both sides assert all three."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a fresh project lists every page ungrouped, in manifest order",
      "manifest": ["/", "/login", "/signup", "/settings"],
      "doc": {
        "view": "rows",
        "routeOrder": [],
        "groups": [],
        "pageLabels": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "flow": ["/", "/login", "/signup", "/settings"],
        "groups": [],
        "ungrouped": ["/", "/login", "/signup", "/settings"]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "the stored flow orders the pages it names, and every page it does not name is appended in manifest order",
      "manifest": ["/", "/login", "/signup", "/settings"],
      "doc": {
        "view": "rows",
        "routeOrder": ["/signup", "/"],
        "groups": [],
        "pageLabels": { "/signup": "Sign up" }
      },
      "expect": {
        "flow": ["/signup", "/", "/login", "/settings"],
        "groups": [],
        "ungrouped": ["/signup", "/", "/login", "/settings"]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a group's pages are listed in flow order, not in the order its own routes array holds",
      "manifest": ["/", "/login", "/signup", "/settings"],
      "doc": {
        "view": "groups",
        "routeOrder": ["/signup", "/login", "/", "/settings"],
        "groups": [{ "id": "g1", "name": "Auth", "routes": ["/login", "/signup"] }],
        "pageLabels": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "flow": ["/signup", "/login", "/", "/settings"],
        "groups": [{ "id": "g1", "name": "Auth", "routes": ["/signup", "/login"] }],
        "ungrouped": ["/", "/settings"]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "groups keep the document's order, and the ungrouped pages are the complement",
      "manifest": ["/", "/login", "/signup", "/settings"],
      "doc": {
        "view": "groups",
        "routeOrder": ["/settings", "/signup", "/login", "/"],
        "groups": [
          { "id": "g1", "name": "Ops", "routes": ["/"] },
          { "id": "g2", "name": "Auth", "routes": ["/login", "/signup"] }
        ],
        "pageLabels": { "/settings": "Preferences" }
      },
      "expect": {
        "flow": ["/settings", "/signup", "/login", "/"],
        "groups": [
          { "id": "g1", "name": "Ops", "routes": ["/"] },
          { "id": "g2", "name": "Auth", "routes": ["/signup", "/login"] }
        ],
        "ungrouped": ["/settings"]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a route two groups claim lists under the first of them, and an empty group keeps its section",
      "manifest": ["/", "/login", "/signup", "/settings"],
      "doc": {
        "view": "groups",
        "routeOrder": [],
        "groups": [
          { "id": "g1", "name": "Auth", "routes": ["/login"] },
          { "id": "g2", "name": "More", "routes": ["/login", "/signup"] },
          { "id": "g3", "name": "Empty", "routes": [] }
        ],
        "pageLabels": {}
      },
      "expect": {
        "flow": ["/", "/login", "/signup", "/settings"],
        "groups": [
          { "id": "g1", "name": "Auth", "routes": ["/login"] },
          { "id": "g2", "name": "More", "routes": ["/signup"] },
          { "id": "g3", "name": "Empty", "routes": [] }
        ],
        "ungrouped": ["/", "/settings"]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a hand-edited document naming a page that is gone, and naming one twice, keeps its grouping and drops what it cannot place",
      "manifest": ["/", "/login"],
      "doc": {
        "view": "groups",
        "routeOrder": ["/settings", "/", "/login", "/"],
        "groups": [
          { "id": "g1", "name": "Auth", "routes": ["/settings"] },
          { "id": "g2", "name": "Home", "routes": ["/"] }
        ],
        "pageLabels": { "/settings": "Preferences" }
      },
      "expect": {
        "flow": ["/", "/login"],
        "groups": [
          { "id": "g1", "name": "Auth", "routes": [] },
          { "id": "g2", "name": "Home", "routes": ["/"] }
        ],
        "ungrouped": ["/login"]
      }
    }
  ]
}
